WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.204
Model storage should balance control with startup performance.

00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:07.084
A managed repository can hold approved model versions, checksums, licenses,

00:00:07.084 --> 00:00:08.248
and configuration metadata.

00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:12.905
Workers can copy approved artifacts into local SSD caches so inference does

00:00:12.905 --> 00:00:16.009
not depend on sustained access to shared storage.

00:00:16.009 --> 00:00:17.949
Define cache size, eviction policy,

00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:24.157
and how a worker verifies that its local copy matches the version advertised to the router.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:28.813
Use explicit version identifiers rather than a mutable label such as latest.

00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:31.529
Model weights, quantization, tokenizer, prompt template, runtime,

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:33.857
and serving parameters together influence behavior.

00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:40.066
Record that combination so results can be reproduced and a problematic release can be rolled back.

00:00:40.066 --> 00:00:43.558
Stage model changes on limited capacity, run representative evaluations,

00:00:43.558 --> 00:00:47.050
and promote only after functional and performance checks pass.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.766
Separate model artifacts from private operational data.

00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:52.482
Prompts, outputs, uploaded files, embeddings, vector indexes,

00:00:52.482 --> 00:00:57.526
and logs can contain sensitive information even when the model weights are public.

00:00:57.526 --> 00:00:59.854
Apply access controls, retention schedules, encryption,

00:00:59.854 --> 00:01:02.571
and backup policies according to data classification.

00:01:02.571 --> 00:01:07.227
Avoid placing private data in a broadly readable model share simply because

00:01:07.227 --> 00:01:09.167
every worker can access it.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:13.435
Back up what cannot be recreated: configuration, routing policy, secrets references,

00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:16.151
evaluation results, metadata, and authorized private datasets.

00:01:16.151 --> 00:01:20.807
Large public model files may be restored from trusted sources if their

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:23.135
exact versions and hashes are recorded.

00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:27.404
Test restoration rather than equating a completed backup job with recoverability.

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:33.224
Storage design succeeds when a new or recovered node can obtain the right model safely,

00:01:33.224 --> 00:01:35.940
start predictably, and avoid exposing unrelated data.
